values ('c3d4e5f6-7a8b-4d42-9f12-2a3b4c5d6e22', 'renaissance-early-modern-literature', 'Renaissance / Early Modern Literature', 'Renaissance / Early Modern Literature studies English writing from roughly the late 15th through the 17th century, with attention to humanism, Reformation conflict, lyric poetry, drama, prose, women writers, empire, print culture, political theology, and Milton. Students read major authors such as Sidney, Spenser, Marlowe, Shakespeare, Donne, Lanyer, Wroth, Jonson, Webster, and Milton while also learning how books, theaters, courts, churches, households, and colonial encounters shaped literary form.');

