reek models shaped English literary form, authorship, and educational ideals."}, {"id": "1e5da821-2075-4cf8-a8e6-72731440d30b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "English Renaissance identity", "children": [{"id": "a400b072-f204-4fff-a42c-84d59c5ad579", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "b5afe911-bd36-4252-bcbe-51cab4fa0b88", "type": "concept", "title": "Tudor monarchy"}, {"id": "81aade6a-3bda-4159-97ab-315c557d1557", "type": "concept", "title": "vernacularization"}, {"id": "0cc4470f-cf58-44a1-823b-128a0ec6987e", "type": "concept", "title": "courtly authorship"}, {"id": "6c81160c-46fd-459a-ba43-ca88ee09a85d", "type": "concept", "title": "patronage"}, {"id": "17a97ee0-b89d-4694-b97c-dd9b5daad0f5", "type": "concept", "title": "Elizabethan settlement"}, {"id": "a4e16210-3cd3-4606-9569-b0c8c96a0e03", "type": "concept", "title": "national mythmaking"}], "description": "The point is to connect national literary ambition with court politics, print expansion, and vernacular prestige."}, {"id": "eb77dff1-d94f-44b9-9226-2c3ac919dc20", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Rhetoric and invention", "children": [{"id": "148ef97c-e527-42a9-aef6-a1c309bd9bc7", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "9362ade3-dde6-4b6c-9ba6-4eed69efaf9e", "type": "concept", "title": "inventio"}, {"id": "5bd1172c-3c59-47cc-8531-3c19e22fbd1e", "type": "concept", "title": "dispositio"}, {"id": "aa3fae9a-b0d0-49ca-a201-2f732e3d7f6e", "type": "concept", "title": "elocutio"}, {"id": "472e2553-fd05-4703-96f3-328898a9c0c0", "type": "concept", "title": "amplification"}, {"id": "05df58f2-a063-4d50-948b-8e3637de4b30", "type": "concept", "title": "figures of speech"}, {"id": "92e74c8b-8504-48b6-b496-449f0c3a0a85", "type": "concept", "title": "commonplaces"}, {"id": "c6adfb29-1b56-4527-83fc-7830ce0c8f9c", "type": "concept", "title": "oration"}, {"id": "6bfd60cf-d91d-4c8b-911a-d1cba9dd996e", "type": "concept", "title": "declamation"}], "description": "Rhetoric gives students the toolkit for seeing how early modern writers build persuasion, style, and argument."}]}, {"id": "5aa1ded1-c656-4bff-9524-d6144b28651e", "type": "topic", "title": "Reformation, Religion, and Early Modern Belief", "description": "Early modern literature is inseparable from religious upheaval. This section shows how theology, worship, conscience, and censorship shaped literary language.", "children": [{"id": "927407fa-97fa-40de-a99e-cabfae6a7b1a", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Reformation conflict and confessional culture", "children": [{"id": "0fa9dac0-85b2-41f8-8eb5-329b9b133a34", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "fbb7042c-7dd8-4e4b-99a7-b610cb54e0b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Protestantism"}, {"id": "a409f1f2-9180-410a-979c-a352f032605c", "type": "concept", "title": "Catholic recusancy"}, {"id": "c1e1e62a-ef51-42c1-91c1-5200c2b5226d", "type": "concept", "title": "Anglican settlement"}, {"id": "5d3a383a-a0a1-4e64-9699-5e7490240048", "type": "concept", "title": "iconoclasm"}, {"id": "00dcb61c-c07c-44c1-9892-ae07b6a61d73", "type": "concept", "title": "martyrdom"}, {"id": "a2d198f3-c733-4c8c-8e49-b1c2427e24fe", "type": "concept", "title": "Foxe's Acts and Monuments"}, {"id": "a9a8b045-a6a1-4382-80e3-151df7ce4f51", "type": "concept", "title": "Thirty-Nine Articles"}], "description": "Students learn how religious change produced new genres of polemic, devotion, and identity formation."}, {"id": "193a1b44-8919-4384-9120-d0bb7efa3176", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Biblical translation and devotional language", "children": [{"id": "39491896-626b-4e48-80c4-26c374e49b76", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "0b5417f7-112c-465c-a9ed-ef0888c4ac05", "type": "concept", "title": "Tyndale Bible"}, {"id": "f0c03006-e846-4de1-bf09-0fdc3c342f30", "type": "concept", "title": "Geneva Bible"}, {"id": "aa74e8b5-008a-4ff3-9d19-f4390152e7b8", "type": "concept", "title": "King James Bible"}, {"id": "cf0be54f-1751-