": "anagnorisis"}, {"id": "6d6c8f27-4ebe-4919-9014-26dd6db588a4", "type": "concept", "title": "catharsis"}, {"id": "7dcb4821-4822-4afa-ab2d-88e65a182fd9", "type": "concept", "title": "tragic temporality"}], "description": "Students learn how tragic form organizes action, error, knowledge, suffering, and audience response."}, {"id": "57d72ca9-f5fa-471c-947b-1fc430927e88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comedy, history, and romance", "children": [{"id": "564874ed-e27d-46e0-8a56-8880d9bead27", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "856b5f44-87f2-4016-8ffd-9374249cb2eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Twelfth Night"}, {"id": "52bd16e4-315d-4ee4-aa4a-2515844fa075", "type": "concept", "title": "Much Ado About Nothing"}, {"id": "134016c2-2a3a-4c0e-a8bd-5490bd962261", "type": "concept", "title": "Henry IV"}, {"id": "1c2fe514-3715-43dc-a6cc-4e1edbf7c79a", "type": "concept", "title": "Richard II"}, {"id": "cfaf999f-4c23-4472-acbf-29e2790a3ed9", "type": "concept", "title": "The Winter's Tale"}, {"id": "b542057f-6f8c-40b1-8403-6f1a9b6b2e82", "type": "concept", "title": "recognition scene"}, {"id": "4ad7dfd2-df30-4024-a141-cb16967a0f6a", "type": "concept", "title": "festive comedy"}, {"id": "fcef5e9a-4c89-492b-9893-207a1063d2a4", "type": "concept", "title": "chronicle history"}], "description": "The point is to see how genre shapes conflict, closure, nationhood, and repair."}, {"id": "39fec8d1-dc7c-4a2a-8170-1fa6f670761b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language, character, and theatricality", "children": [{"id": "83dbbc38-e0a3-4ee5-8e6e-3387eb0e9cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "d1072302-5265-4851-bcb1-78e6f84c3713", "type": "concept", "title": "soliloquy"}, {"id": "b9a4bc30-ddb5-47c2-8ade-2816d526dde3", "type": "concept", "title": "aside"}, {"id": "6f5c8089-81a1-4bbe-a60c-8bff0097548a", "type": "concept", "title": "blank verse"}, {"id": "a7fe1630-51a0-408d-9bfd-282eeeeb3803", "type": "concept", "title": "prose switch"}, {"id": "a9adacd6-49d5-4c4d-bb1f-93942be3d535", "type": "concept", "title": "metatheater"}, {"id": "6c0f7ab4-7b1b-4a42-a984-6af05b03235f", "type": "concept", "title": "wordplay"}, {"id": "5981b511-edda-4204-91d4-f18133827ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "rhetorical question"}, {"id": "fd6ea981-8a5e-41f5-ae26-cde39f9a02ba", "type": "concept", "title": "cue script"}], "description": "Students practice close reading Shakespearean speech as performance, not just page text."}]}, {"id": "67375b46-b429-4e41-a8c7-085e3a54293c", "type": "topic", "title": "Renaissance Drama Beyond Shakespeare", "description": "A world-class course must decenter Shakespeare enough for students to see the full theatrical ecosystem: companies, genres, rivals, collaborators, and city audiences.", "children": [{"id": "e04ba2e6-785a-4f7b-adf2-71b24a3e9e75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jonson, comedy, and satire", "children": [{"id": "78236f15-9944-408e-98a9-6fdac39f3dae", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "daa3e5d7-e4fc-4a97-84d7-7aa3239dc621", "type": "concept", "title": "Ben Jonson"}, {"id": "cd0e7a6e-21fe-4ba6-92f8-56ac3ea41d0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Volpone"}, {"id": "2a90cc25-91e1-4fce-b782-6400d81e9639", "type": "concept", "title": "The Alchemist"}, {"id": "18cd795d-1d17-4b3d-ac39-4591567be31a", "type": "concept", "title": "humours"}, {"id": "d145bca8-b4c3-444d-8308-ffdd2cbd8c43", "type": "concept", "title": "city comedy"}, {"id": "ec375240-97c8-4b5f-a8b6-5a4c49904eec", "type": "concept", "title": "satire"}, {"id": "ef6594dc-ff1c-4a9e-a8e8-de0673be2c4c", "type": "concept", "title": "gulling"}, {"id": "e82a9578-1489-49ab-b9c3-dc188835ef25", "type": "concept", "title": "social type"}], "description": "Students learn how humoral theory, social types, and urban satire structure comic drama."}, {"id": "51b84e20-3f76-49dd-9535-c0beac5b0edf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenge tragedy and dark drama", "children": [{"id": "bd518ff3-3424-43f4-86fa-f9f