hnologies, and shared labor."}]}, {"id": "c17f9512-f0e4-4038-aaee-31a00a59ca22", "type": "topic", "title": "Early Modern Prose, Rhetoric, and Print Culture", "description": "This section expands the course beyond canonical poetry and drama into prose genres, print publics, and the material life of texts.", "children": [{"id": "17af15e2-8351-41e6-bbbe-d0ba1edce286", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essays, sermons, pamphlets, and polemic", "children": [{"id": "4cea97b9-7c7f-4c33-9437-bdf3c81f8fae", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "d2dc48bc-730d-4e8d-b471-5a84ca177534", "type": "concept", "title": "Francis Bacon"}, {"id": "8f65b4d4-1589-47eb-826b-90353f504d16", "type": "concept", "title": "Michel de Montaigne"}, {"id": "40e08da9-7ccb-4562-a28b-ca151d787ba9", "type": "concept", "title": "sermon"}, {"id": "f882f5fe-71e8-4bd0-be4f-e313de78515c", "type": "concept", "title": "homily"}, {"id": "62358a10-1a89-4be2-9983-44f17423386f", "type": "concept", "title": "pamphlet"}, {"id": "99d6a3ba-1c0a-405d-9738-6bb063c1eff3", "type": "concept", "title": "newsbook"}, {"id": "66be16dc-ed33-48f0-8b4a-2d36a14be735", "type": "concept", "title": "polemical prose"}, {"id": "e17f8110-8053-4eb7-b2bc-5ad1a2e62f15", "type": "concept", "title": "aphorism"}], "description": "Students learn how prose forms intervene in public argument, religion, science, and politics."}, {"id": "d7d9b9d6-6b5a-4ab3-a644-7d08eea1164c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Book history and paratexts", "children": [{"id": "f4c564f7-0828-45fa-99f4-3f0f96971418", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "1c966e17-fe4d-458d-a628-85a0a33691ff", "type": "concept", "title": "quarto"}, {"id": "825f53ae-15d5-47ce-b0a8-bdcabd80cd8a", "type": "concept", "title": "folio"}, {"id": "2aecd68a-c22f-4ff5-9909-e043258c2ee0", "type": "concept", "title": "octavo"}, {"id": "5d7ef482-401d-4bc9-804e-3c5c9474264e", "type": "concept", "title": "title page"}, {"id": "9ef9ac19-3490-4629-a329-