": "Tyranny, counsel, and resistance", "children": [{"id": "b62cbdfd-1937-439f-9603-9029c7641849", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "1bdbaedf-658b-4944-804c-e0add6888b12", "type": "concept", "title": "mirror for magistrates"}, {"id": "053adf2b-5c92-4d62-9692-bec00edbedd2", "type": "concept", "title": "reason of state"}, {"id": "ccffb31b-2710-44a6-9e7d-1225b327f458", "type": "concept", "title": "Machiavelli"}, {"id": "85ed78d7-0c64-4890-be17-53cce2ac93e9", "type": "concept", "title": "counselor"}, {"id": "590bdc11-1686-440c-8e7a-a6dc4f491f61", "type": "concept", "title": "tyrant"}, {"id": "c2170547-db20-4c2a-a604-f426fb4f08c2", "type": "concept", "title": "rebellion"}, {"id": "1f478f30-ce2d-425c-adbb-743998ad0870", "type": "concept", "title": "obedience"}, {"id": "1fc71b9f-78b7-4f31-839c-c5158e0b3d8b", "type": "concept", "title": "resistance theory"}], "description": "The gist is to see political argument embedded in tragedy, history, prose, and allegory."}, {"id": "b5bbebca-3901-475d-8682-d64fb2a2febf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Civil war and republican thought", "children": [{"id": "660efd78-a90c-4020-bc22-738973bd9560", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "051e37c5-54ee-4003-ad70-553686758bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Long Parliament"}, {"id": "a28d1bb8-0be0-423e-a74d-5fbdbd4fa27f", "type": "concept", "title": "regicide"}, {"id": "012f0e2c-03ad-43b3-a3fa-16fcf53edd22", "type": "concept", "title": "commonwealth"}, {"id": "d8a09365-7ade-4f38-ad9b-4de187fdd9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Levellers"}, {"id": "3ed8e922-938a-41aa-abff-e2fc99c2d858", "type": "concept", "title": "royalism"}, {"id": "6d6f065b-8eb1-410a-bfab-d8162a0ea0ed", "type": "concept", "title": "republicanism"}, {"id": "bcdd0dcf-f64b-42e0-a807-12d37a321423", "type": "concept", "title": "pamphlet debate"}, {"id": "066ec85a-0f6f-4b5a-b1d3-e7008f6140bb", "type": "concept", "title": "restoration"}], "description": "Students trace the pressure that religious and political conflict places on literary form."}]}, {"id": "e7ab1c0c-8986-40fa-a586-b79cf214531d", "type": "topic", "title": "Milton, Civil War, and Seventeenth-Century Crisis", "description": "Milton anchors the course's final movement from Renaissance humanist ambition to revolutionary politics and epic theology.", "children": [{"id": "0a0b6701-b59b-470b-870e-9484e5de16ab", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Paradise Lost and epic theology", "children": [{"id": "93111562-c64c-4078-ba43-bae16e14140a", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "68cbafd5-0ed6-408d-9630-24097d8d7c84", "type": "concept", "title": "Satan"}, {"id": "1e06234b-a909-4c64-9299-e95283921430", "type": "concept", "title": "Adam"}, {"id": "5dfc40bc-8bbf-4b9e-82c6-4e995784202d", "type": "concept", "title": "Eve"}, {"id": "77fd64a7-b390-425d-97eb-dfee5f2148c7", "type": "concept", "title": "free will"}, {"id": "ffe750a1-2110-4d45-b614-469591b5c7c9", "type": "concept", "title": "obedience"}, {"id": "4ef84dcd-dfa8-430e-847d-46ab91e42215", "type": "concept", "title": "felix culpa"}, {"id": "3fdba297-9144-447e-9ade-fe92154ec6a6", "type": "concept", "title": "invocation"}, {"id": "f2061a94-5a75-4505-aed1-9515980fdaad", "type": "concept", "title": "blank verse epic"}], "description": "Students learn how Milton reworks biblical narrative, classical epic, and theological debate."}, {"id": "fd011d2c-8653-4705-b81a-84d2afa63927", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Miltonic prose and public argument", "children": [{"id": "7d3a5de5-5989-4e71-a62b-04d7ff2405ba", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "d7b58ec7-2e11-4ca4-b05b-4a16800a6ad2", "type": "concept", "title": "Areopagitica"}, {"id": "c5d75751-15e2-4e9a-a082-b4f4ec86e0dc", "type": "concept", "title": "Tenure of Kings and Magistrates"}, {"id": "180f26dc-3f7d-44c8-9f86-19e251985fc1", "type": "concept", "title": "divorce tracts"}, {"id": "195abab2-bb29-4210-9266-209fe39cfbe0", "type": "con