lizabethan Ireland"}], "description": "Students confront the imperial politics behind Spenser's literary project."}]}, {"id": "eb3628b4-7447-4fc6-91b4-c37769ff8bdf", "type": "topic", "title": "Sidney, Poetics, and the Defense of Literature", "description": "Sidney helps students understand how early modern writers theorized fiction, ethical instruction, and imaginative power.", "children": [{"id": "fdc9caed-6f18-497c-a126-4f5ccf82cc22", "type": "subtopic", "title": "The Defence of Poesy", "children": [{"id": "792a9b7e-d31e-498d-adc6-ca14cc07d28f", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "0285f743-2d7c-404d-8cf1-0304f2b5d2c9", "type": "concept", "title": "mimesis"}, {"id": "55d3432a-c25b-4dd9-b56b-aa4e8b6bb964", "type": "concept", "title": "golden world"}, {"id": "5a404c56-23c8-4b38-8262-525903d0b796", "type": "concept", "title": "speaking picture"}, {"id": "74150467-6575-4a85-a578-57eb50da4d5d", "type": "concept", "title": "delight and teach"}, {"id": "5409a91a-b0b3-4779-b011-09088b812b84", "type": "concept", "title": "poet-maker"}, {"id": "3e18dfa3-5f28-49ec-aab0-06e7f647ceae", "type": "concept", "title": "fictionality"}, {"id": "00c0a6dc-377b-475d-a9db-2c9dc971f5f5", "type": "concept", "title": "ethical example"}], "description": "Students learn the period's strongest argument for literature as moral philosophy in action."}, {"id": "afd78e26-2989-4a86-bbed-79d7cabfbf8c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Arcadia and prose romance", "children": [{"id": "0dee6cff-198b-4045-9af2-14c869c1c66f", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "8f09db15-fe0d-4440-9eed-e65c60def41a", "type": "concept", "title": "Old Arcadia"}, {"id": "7ccdd5eb-7ef4-4371-a4b1-2936ff4401f2", "type": "concept", "title": "New Arcadia"}, {"id": "4c550738-3ddf-4df0-97de-63bcae892aaa", "type": "concept", "title": "pastoral"}, {"id": "91ee4ebb-c5b6-41f4-9e9f-c56845fafc11", "type": "concept", "title": "romance"}, {"id": "77b5501a-cb29-4f37-8640-438f710db8e6