 "title": "anagnorisis"}, {"id": "6d6c8f27-4ebe-4919-9014-26dd6db588a4", "type": "concept", "title": "catharsis"}, {"id": "7dcb4821-4822-4afa-ab2d-88e65a182fd9", "type": "concept", "title": "tragic temporality"}], "description": "Students learn how tragic form organizes action, error, knowledge, suffering, and audience response."}, {"id": "57d72ca9-f5fa-471c-947b-1fc430927e88", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Comedy, history, and romance", "children": [{"id": "564874ed-e27d-46e0-8a56-8880d9bead27", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "856b5f44-87f2-4016-8ffd-9374249cb2eb", "type": "concept", "title": "Twelfth Night"}, {"id": "52bd16e4-315d-4ee4-aa4a-2515844fa075", "type": "concept", "title": "Much Ado About Nothing"}, {"id": "134016c2-2a3a-4c0e-a8bd-5490bd962261", "type": "concept", "title": "Henry IV"}, {"id": "1c2fe514-3715-43dc-a6cc-4e1edbf7c79a", "type": "concept", "title": "Richard II"}, {"id": "cfaf999f-4c23-4472-acbf-29e2790a3ed9", "type": "concept", "title": "The Winter's Tale"}, {"id": "b542057f-6f8c-40b1-8403-6f1a9b6b2e82", "type": "concept", "title": "recognition scene"}, {"id": "4ad7dfd2-df30-4024-a141-cb16967a0f6a", "type": "concept", "title": "festive comedy"}, {"id": "fcef5e9a-4c89-492b-9893-207a1063d2a4", "type": "concept", "title": "chronicle history"}], "description": "The point is to see how genre shapes conflict, closure, nationhood, and repair."}, {"id": "39fec8d1-dc7c-4a2a-8170-1fa6f670761b", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Language, character, and theatricality", "children": [{"id": "83dbbc38-e0a3-4ee5-8e6e-3387eb0e9cca", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "d1072302-5265-4851-bcb1-78e6f84c3713", "type": "concept", "title": "soliloquy"}, {"id": "b9a4bc30-ddb5-47c2-8ade-2816d526dde3", "type": "concept", "title": "aside"}, {"id": "6f5c8089-81a1-4bbe-a60c-8bff0097548a", "type": "concept", "title": "blank verse"}, {"id": "a7fe1630-51a0-408d-9bfd-282eeeeb3803", "type": "concept", "title": "prose switch"}, {"id": "a9adacd6-49d5-4c4d-bb1f-93942be3d535", "type": "concept", "title": "metatheater"}, {"id": "6c0f7ab4-7b1b-4a42-a984-6af05b03235f", "type": "concept", "title": "wordplay"}, {"id": "5981b511-edda-4204-91d4-f18133827ef5", "type": "concept", "title": "rhetorical question"}, {"id": "fd6ea981-8a5e-41f5-ae26-cde39f9a02ba", "type": "concept", "title": "cue script"}], "description": "Students practice close reading Shakespearean speech as performance, not just page text."}]}, {"id": "67375b46-b429-4e41-a8c7-085e3a54293c", "type": "topic", "title": "Renaissance Drama Beyond Shakespeare", "description": "A world-class course must decenter Shakespeare enough for students to see the full theatrical ecosystem: companies, genres, rivals, collaborators, and city audiences.", "children": [{"id": "e04ba2e6-785a-4f7b-adf2-71b24a3e9e75", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Jonson, comedy, and satire", "children": [{"id": "78236f15-9944-408e-98a9-6fdac39f3dae", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "daa3e5d7-e4fc-4a97-84d7-7aa3239dc621", "type": "concept", "title": "Ben Jonson"}, {"id": "cd0e7a6e-21fe-4ba6-92f8-56ac3ea41d0b", "type": "concept", "title": "Volpone"}, {"id": "2a90cc25-91e1-4fce-b782-6400d81e9639", "type": "concept", "title": "The Alchemist"}, {"id": "18cd795d-1d17-4b3d-ac39-4591567be31a", "type": "concept", "title": "humours"}, {"id": "d145bca8-b4c3-444d-8308-ffdd2cbd8c43", "type": "concept", "title": "city comedy"}, {"id": "ec375240-97c8-4b5f-a8b6-5a4c49904eec", "type": "concept", "title": "satire"}, {"id": "ef6594dc-ff1c-4a9e-a8e8-de0673be2c4c", "type": "concept", "title": "gulling"}, {"id": "e82a9578-1489-49ab-b9c3-dc188835ef25", "type": "concept", "title": "social type"}], "description": "Students learn how humoral theory, social types, and urban satire structure comic drama."}, {"id": "51b84e20-3f76-49dd-9535-c0beac5b0edf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Revenge tragedy and dark drama", "children": [{"id": "bd518ff3-3424-43f4-86fa-f9f82737368c", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "afb74d68-8869-4058-b81f-afc7b7f406a8", "type": "concept", "title": "Thomas Kyd"}, {"id": "be30e1d0-b222-451a-8bb9-c99560610ddb", "type": "concept", "title": "The Spanish Tragedy"}, {"id": "7eba0714-a1fe-4bb3-8e2c-00db8f2f4ebe", "type": "concept", "title": "Webster"}, {"id": "e18641f3-34ae-498f-b279-e46e80dce410", "type": "concept", "title": "The Duchess of Malfi"}, {"id": "e10827f8-fc19-4d9f-b7c4-51fa615c5422", "type": "concept", "title": "Middleton"}, {"id": "628e02c2-0a27-471e-984a-7c48b0a6e49b", "type": "concept", "title": "revenge plot"}, {"id": "162d6ad1-3e96-4522-9b03-eb51c205abfb", "type": "concept", "title": "ghost"}, {"id": "ee4d2910-b07d-4023-8488-f12f3c7beb55", "type": "concept", "title": "malcontent"}], "description": "The gist is to understand sensational drama as moral inquiry, political critique, and theatrical machine."}, {"id": "ccaa27a1-7545-4b49-b753-9543c740dd3c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Masque, collaboration, and theatrical institutions", "children": [{"id": "a51c3ebc-a1b1-4bfc-8b4e-4b7132b6d5f4", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "4f90a6b6-9c95-491c-b64f-45ab206dcdfb", "type": "concept", "title": "court masque"}, {"id": "82004cb2-1399-4e1f-8bd1-9410cde226d3", "type": "concept", "title": "Inigo Jones"}, {"id": "8159bb52-f179-41e2-a6f5-bd5ca398925a", "type": "concept", "title": "Blackfriars"}, {"id": "16aa5cc8-265b-4318-831d-730b93d514d2", "type": "concept", "title": "Globe"}, {"id": "4f9a770e-b896-49c5-98dc-7bd1236b38e9", "type": "concept", "title": "boy companies"}, {"id": "2745cb6e-fdec-48b9-a08a-8e9566fa0fbb", "type": "concept", "title": "Lord Chamberlain's Men"}, {"id": "7e5e8810-7599-43a2-bca5-0585cdd9438b", "type": "concept", "title": "collaborative authorship"}, {"id": "e5e97929-77c0-4c41-a539-9ddf0d37897a", "type": "concept", "title": "promptbook"}], "description": "Students see drama as produced by companies, patrons, technologies, and shared labor."}]}, {"id": "c17f9512-f0e4-4038-aaee-31a00a59ca22", "type": "topic", "title": "Early Modern Prose, Rhetoric, and Print Culture", "description": "This section expands the course beyond canonical poetry and drama into prose genres, print publics, and the material life of texts.", "children": [{"id": "17af15e2-8351-41e6-bbbe-d0ba1edce286", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essays, sermons, pamphlets, and polemic", "children": [{"id": "4cea97b9-7c7f-4c33-9437-bdf3c81f8fae", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "d2dc48bc-730d-4e8d-b471-5a84ca177534", "type": "concept", "title": "Francis Bacon"}, {"id": "8f65b4d4-1589-47eb-826b-90353f504d16", "type": "concept", "title": "Michel de Montaigne"}, {"id": "40e08da9-7ccb-4562-a28b-ca151d787ba9", "type": "concept", "title": "sermon"}, {"id": "f882f5fe-71e8-4bd0-be4f-e313de78515c", "type": "concept", "title": "homily"}, {"id": "62358a10-1a89-4be2-9983-44f17423386f", "type": "concept", "title": "pamphlet"}, {"id": "99d6a3ba-1c0a-405d-9738-6bb063c1eff3", "type": "concept", "title": "newsbook"}, {"id": "66be16dc-ed33-48f0-8b4a-2d36a14be735", "type": "concept", "title": "polemical prose"}, {"id": "e17f8110-8053-4eb7-b2bc-5ad1a2e62f15", "type": "concept", "title": "aphorism"}], "description": "Students learn how prose forms intervene in public argument, religion, science, and politics."}, {"id": "d7d9b9d6-6b5a-4ab3-a644-7d08eea1164c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Book history and paratexts", "children": [{"id": "f4c564f7-0828-45fa-99f4-3f0f96971418", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "1c966e17-fe4d-458d-a628-85a0a33691ff", "type": "concept", "title": "quarto"}, {"id": "825f53ae-15d5-47ce-b0a8-bdcabd80cd8a", "type": "concept", "title": "folio"}, {"id": "2aecd68a-c22f-4ff5-9909-e043258c2ee0", "type": "concept", "title": "octavo"}, {"id": "5d7ef482-401d-4bc9-804e-3c5c9474264e", "type": "concept", "title": "title page"}, {"id": "9ef9ac19-3490-4629-a329-b39a41e2fe56", "type": "concept", "title": "dedication"}, {"id": "70eaabf2-df9e-455a-a68b-88f0c563f561", "type": "concept", "title": "preface"}, {"id": "f62a9ca9-3482-411f-bd88-69a0d2383a10", "type": "concept", "title": "errata"}, {"id": "0deac58d-6ade-4337-bbf1-dd9d64d919df", "type": "concept", "title": "marginal note"}], "description": "The point is to read title pages, dedications, prefaces, and marginalia as part of meaning."}, {"id": "40aea7af-51e8-4344-8ce1-fe5d39551460", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Readers, stationers, and censorship", "children": [{"id": "913109d4-f802-45d2-91ae-d456f4b0fe01", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "ba25fe66-48d1-4371-99fc-6c79397f5b87", "type": "concept", "title": "Stationers' Register"}, {"id": "4624fe5d-700b-4425-b6df-80492399d7cb", "type": "concept", "title": "printer"}, {"id": "d10ce0bd-1beb-459c-86c4-6af3baab5789", "type": "concept", "title": "bookseller"}, {"id": "d36308c7-494c-4696-b994-e8c764707abd", "type": "concept", "title": "patron"}, {"id": "1c8bcb33-3ed7-452e-8b8b-ddebfc556fcd", "type": "concept", "title": "license"}, {"id": "4d7d69bc-8e34-4d7b-a75c-539be6fefbb1", "type": "concept", "title": "blackletter"}, {"id": "4350df84-c20b-49bd-82bd-28c336276b38", "type": "concept", "title": "reading publics"}, {"id": "59a0ccbb-5093-4d40-835e-4c0cd0eb98cd", "type": "concept", "title": "commonplace book"}], "description": "Students understand literature as shaped by markets, licensing, and reading communities."}]}, {"id": "ff5f99a3-0861-4641-bb2f-6826570733ca", "type": "topic", "title": "Women Writers, Gender, and Household Politics", "description": "This section treats gender not as an add-on but as a central framework for authorship, authority, labor, religion, and literary form.", "children": [{"id": "f727f5b3-b39e-40f0-bf9d-9655c296c298", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Women authors and publication", "children": [{"id": "227a9ce5-3b5d-4eb0-ba11-eec0a6d9829c", "type": "concept", "titl