": "subtopic", "title": "Gendered voice and revision", "children": [{"id": "66e852e9-d127-4678-b74b-b765d3851abe", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "84c2fc05-fab0-46d1-a75e-43ae6b4f6c72", "type": "concept", "title": "Eve apology"}, {"id": "45ea34ed-08d9-4293-be1b-a4521b1c91b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Salve Deus Rex Judaeorum"}, {"id": "1a94e3e3-93d5-4bec-9679-399085b0b6b5", "type": "concept", "title": "Pamphilia"}, {"id": "5cf377ec-4788-4d43-a80c-6d892fd5cd39", "type": "concept", "title": "Mariam"}, {"id": "1ed1c7ec-2de7-4bf1-b7da-69b60e946416", "type": "concept", "title": "female complaint"}, {"id": "51736324-d8d5-4f02-91c5-e1d902faef15", "type": "concept", "title": "prophecy"}, {"id": "af76fe0b-e8cb-4dee-bb7d-ca9addfb8315", "type": "concept", "title": "counter-blazon"}, {"id": "941951c4-dc35-4419-a105-efd05e187521", "type": "concept", "title": "authorial self-defense"}], "description": "Students examine how women writers revise scripture, romance, sonnet convention, and political speech."}]}, {"id": "1bb7acea-6a88-43e3-9653-decc7dd8f78b", "type": "topic", "title": "Race, Empire, Travel, and Encounter", "description": "Early modern texts register expanding contact with Africa, the Americas, Ireland, the Ottoman world, and Asia. Students learn the vocabulary and violence of early imperial imagination.", "children": [{"id": "6d26616f-cb9a-4fea-9bac-d0c1caa3328c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Travel writing and colonial discourse", "children": [{"id": "4977bf06-eaad-428d-9ef0-6d6fc4abb9b0", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "2493a6b5-be94-49aa-9499-78ac9fc382ff", "type": "concept", "title": "Richard Hakluyt"}, {"id": "34edbce1-e331-4270-96f8-15d0a1906582", "type": "concept", "title": "New World"}, {"id": "b18d303f-c0ca-446e-bd5f-ad7f5e77b4aa", "type": "concept", "title": "Virginia"}, {"id": "bf3e7d74-242f-4637-9f51-0a32a679b420", "type": "concept", "title": "plantation"}, {"id": "b07d4da9-6d98-4fe