", "title": "charter companies"}, {"id": "609603cc-137d-4e5c-91ae-14dd209427a4", "type": "concept", "title": "mercantilism"}, {"id": "cee284c1-7932-4d1a-ac36-1c8839e6053d", "type": "concept", "title": "plantation"}, {"id": "bc91b44f-52e6-495a-89bb-80b3d0de60f2", "type": "concept", "title": "civility"}, {"id": "67c1d95e-0009-4ef9-8a9d-3d26dccf66ba", "type": "concept", "title": "barbarism"}, {"id": "7513a1c5-fb9a-4456-8d5c-024463327351", "type": "concept", "title": "imperial providence"}], "description": "Students connect English literature to conquest, trade, extraction, and settler colonial language."}]}, {"id": "2ea8939d-6e83-4f10-adbf-251e6384c6df", "type": "topic", "title": "Political Theology, Monarchy, and Sovereignty", "description": "Literature became a place to imagine obedience, resistance, tyranny, counsel, and the sacred aura of power.", "children": [{"id": "51df013b-1dc7-4a3e-8426-7a643ba3ee84", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Kingship and legitimacy", "children": [{"id": "1021fc73-5872-4918-b191-9c1472a3a434", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "908828ed-c8b2-4000-9c12-ce2b844fc4b9", "type": "concept", "title": "divine right"}, {"id": "4f87f03f-fcc2-439f-a5df-6c4a00b7ef42", "type": "concept", "title": "succession"}, {"id": "05160ed7-9c93-476e-8a43-15546c699f66", "type": "concept", "title": "Elizabeth I"}, {"id": "7bfddbb5-2cbe-49eb-a86e-fbea8b5f2355", "type": "concept", "title": "James I"}, {"id": "6514fb62-3417-41a8-aa75-7d6c2d3f73c0", "type": "concept", "title": "two bodies of the king"}, {"id": "2a45bdaa-17ce-448f-8b46-73ef854db465", "type": "concept", "title": "royal progress"}, {"id": "b0354a76-23b1-4ac1-84b3-1fb5fb795c36", "type": "concept", "title": "court masque"}, {"id": "38890f13-76a2-4524-9580-e816a71de387", "type": "concept", "title": "coronation"}], "description": "Students learn how monarchy was defended, staged, questioned, and mythologized."}, {"id": "cce4f259-8412-4177-8bc2-da45293d397c", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Tyranny, counsel, and resistance", "children": [{"id": "b62cbdfd-1937-439f-9603-9029c7641849", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "1bdbaedf-658b-4944-804c-e0add6888b12", "type": "concept", "title": "mirror for magistrates"}, {"id": "053adf2b-5c92-4d62-9692-bec00edbedd2", "type": "concept", "title": "reason of state"}, {"id": "ccffb31b-2710-44a6-9e7d-1225b327f458", "type": "concept", "title": "Machiavelli"}, {"id": "85ed78d7-0c64-4890-be17-53cce2ac93e9", "type": "concept", "title": "counselor"}, {"id": "590bdc11-1686-440c-8e7a-a6dc4f491f61", "type": "concept", "title": "tyrant"}, {"id": "c2170547-db20-4c2a-a604-f426fb4f08c2", "type": "concept", "title": "rebellion"}, {"id": "1f478f30-ce2d-425c-adbb-743998ad0870", "type": "concept", "title": "obedience"}, {"id": "1fc71b9f-78b7-4f31-839c-c5158e0b3d8b", "type": "concept", "title": "resistance theory"}], "description": "The gist is to see political argument embedded in tragedy, history, prose, and allegory."}, {"id": "b5bbebca-3901-475d-8682-d64fb2a2febf", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Civil war and republican thought", "children": [{"id": "660efd78-a90c-4020-bc22-738973bd9560", "type": "concept", "title": "Specific terms and topics:"}, {"id": "051e37c5-54ee-4003-ad70-553686758bee", "type": "concept", "title": "Long Parliament"}, {"id": "a28d1bb8-0be0-423e-a74d-5fbdbd4fa27f", "type": "concept", "title": "regicide"}, {"id": "012f0e2c-03ad-43b3-a3fa-16fcf53edd22", "type": "concept", "title": "commonwealth"}, {"id": "d8a09365-7ade-4f38-ad9b-4de187fdd9d4", "type": "concept", "title": "Levellers"}, {"id": "3ed8e922-938a-41aa-abff-e2fc99c2d858", "type": "concept", "title": "royalism"}, {"id": "6d6f065b-8eb1-410a-bfab-d8162a0ea0ed", "type": "concept", "title": "republicanism"}, {"id": "bcdd0dcf-f64b-42e0-a807-12d37a321423", "type": "concept", "title": "pamphlet debate"}, {"id": "066ec85a-0f6f-4b5a-b1d3-e7008f6140bb", "type": "concept", "title": "restoration"}], "description": "Students 